KNOWNBUG
shared-loop-variable6.sv
--bound 0
^file .* line \d+: `Verilog::\$root\.main\.count' has multiple drivers$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^EXIT=2$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.o == 4'b0000: REFUTED$
--
Correctness hole from the type-based exemption. 'count' is genuine
two-driver STATE: it is written by two separate clocked always blocks
and read by a third, so it is a real multiple-driver conflict that
should be rejected with "`...count' has multiple drivers" / CONVERSION
ERROR (the desired output in the match section above). But the exemption
in verilog_rtl_buildert::commit suppresses the multiple-driver check for
ALL 'integer'-typed symbols, so the conflict is currently silently
accepted and the design elaborates (property REFUTED -- the output in
the '--' section below, which must NOT appear once this is fixed). A
liveness-based exemption would not mask this, since 'count' is read
outside the writing blocks.
